.TH PVE\-SDN\-HEALTHCHECK 8 "2026-07-03" "1.1.0" "Proxmox VE Tools"
.SH NAME
pve\-sdn\-healthcheck \- validate the underlay and overlay network of a Proxmox VE SDN cluster
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pve\-sdn\-healthcheck
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B pve\-sdn\-healthcheck
.RB [ \-\-node
.IR a , b , c ]
.RB [ \-\-only
.IR underlay | overlay ]
.RB [ \-\-all ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B pve\-sdn\-healthcheck
.RB [ \-\-fix
.RI [ CHECKS ]]
.RB [ \-\-apply ]
.RB [ \-\-yes ]
.br
.B pve\-sdn\-healthcheck
.B \-\-explain
.I CHECK
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pve\-sdn\-healthcheck
is a strictly read\-only validator for the network layer of a hyper\-converged
Proxmox VE cluster running FRR with BGP\-EVPN/VXLAN (the Proxmox SDN stack).
It connects to every cluster node over SSH, runs a battery of underlay and
overlay checks on each, and aggregates the results into an operator\-friendly,
fail\-first report with a single cluster\-wide verdict.
.PP
The tool is portable: every site\-specific entity (node list, VTEP peers, L3
VNIs/VRFs, external BGP peers) is
.B auto\-discovered
from the live system, so it runs unmodified on any PVE + FRR/EVPN cluster.
Nodes without an SDN overlay are detected and their overlay/forwarding checks
are skipped rather than failed.
.PP
Each check is classified by severity \(em
.BR OK ", " WARN ", or " FAIL
\(em and the process exits with the highest severity seen, using the Nagios
convention so the tool can drive monitoring (LibreNMS, Zabbix, Icinga) and CI.
.SS Checks performed
.B Underlay:
IPv4 forwarding (runtime + persistence), FRR daemon health, physical link
state, NIC errors/drops, link flapping, SFP/QSFP optic DOM (temperature and
optical power, on lit ports only), bond/LACP state, MTU headroom (VXLAN
transport must exceed the overlay MTU by at least 50 bytes), internal
BGP\-EVPN fabric sessions, per\-VRF external BGP peering (IPv4 and IPv6), VTEP
reachability, and Ceph network health.
.PP
.B Overlay:
presence of expected L2/L3 VNIs (control plane vs. kernel), EVPN route
population, anycast\-gateway/IRB state, L3\-VNI FDB completeness (distinguishing
a real symmetric\-IRB black\-hole from benign on\-demand absence), and RIB/FIB
consistency (catching a stuck/phantom zebra route).
.PP
.B Plumbing:
each running guest's NIC chain
.RB ( tap / veth " \(-> " fwbr / fwpr / fwln " \(-> " vnet / vmbr )
is verified intact, mirroring the detection logic of
.BR pve\-vmnic\-fix (8).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-node " " \fIa\fR,\fIb\fR,\fIc\fR
Check only the listed nodes (host names or IPs, optionally
.IR user @ host ).
Default: auto\-discover all cluster members.
.TP
.BR \-\-only " " \fIunderlay\fR|\fIoverlay\fR
Run only one layer of checks.
.TP
.BR \-\-check " " \fINAME\fR[,\fINAME\fR...]
Run only the named checks (see
.BR \-\-list\-checks ).
.TP
.BR \-\-explain " " \fICHECK\fR
Print what a check validates, why it matters, and how WARN/FAIL are decided,
then exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-drop\-window " " \fISEC\fR
Sample live NIC
.BR rx_dropped / tx_dropped
deltas over
.I SEC
seconds for the
.B iface_errors
check (default: 5).  All live NICs are sampled before one shared sleep and then
sampled again, so multi\-NIC hosts get accurate per\-interface deltas without
sleeping once per NIC.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Also show
.B OK
lines (by default only WARN and FAIL are shown, plus a hidden\-count note).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit a machine\-readable JSON document (schema_version 1.0) for monitoring
ingestion instead of the human report.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI colour (also auto\-disabled when stdout is not a terminal).
.TP
.B \-\-list\-checks
Print the check catalogue and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-fix " [" \fICHECKS\fR ]
Preview safe, allow\-listed auto\-remediations for any detected, fixable issues.
With no argument, all allow\-listed checks are considered. This only
.B previews
\(em nothing is changed.
.TP
.B \-\-apply
Execute the previewed fixes. Implies
.BR \-\-fix ,
requires root, and appends an audit record to
.IR /var/log/pve\-sdn\-healthcheck\-fix.log .
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Skip the interactive confirmation for
.BR \-\-apply
(required when running non\-interactively).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the built\-in help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version number and exit.
.SH AUTO-REMEDIATION
.B pve\-sdn\-healthcheck
is read\-only by default. The optional
.B \-\-fix
facility is strictly opt\-in and limited to a small allow\-list of safe,
idempotent, locally\-scoped repairs:
.IP \(bu 3
.B ip_forward
\(em set and persist
.B net.ipv4.ip_forward=1
(and the matching forwarding sysctls) in
.IR /etc/sysctl.d/ .
.IP \(bu 3
.B vmnic_plumbing
\(em repair a broken guest NIC chain by delegating to
.BR pve\-vmnic\-fix (8).
.IP \(bu 3
.B frr_daemon
\(em enable FRR at boot
.RB ( "systemctl enable frr" ;
no restart).
.PP
Everything else \(em BGP/EVPN sessions, zebra/FRR restarts, MTU, optics,
bonding \(em is reported with guidance but
.B never
changed automatically, because such actions require human judgement and can
widen an outage. Fixes preview by default;
.B \-\-apply
is required to execute and is logged.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check the whole cluster (auto\-discovered nodes):
.PP
.RS
.nf
pve\-sdn\-healthcheck
.fi
.RE
.PP
Only the overlay, on two named nodes, showing every check:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pve\-sdn\-healthcheck \-\-node pve01,pve02 \-\-only overlay \-\-all
.fi
.RE
.PP
Explain a specific check:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pve\-sdn\-healthcheck \-\-explain l3vni_fdb
.fi
.RE
.PP
Preview, then apply, safe auto\-fixes:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pve\-sdn\-healthcheck \-\-fix
pve\-sdn\-healthcheck \-\-fix ip_forward \-\-apply \-\-yes
.fi
.RE
.PP
Feed a monitoring system:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pve\-sdn\-healthcheck \-\-json | jq .counts
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run from a management host that is not a cluster member, via a jump host:
.PP
.RS
.nf
SDN_NODES='root@10.0.0.4 root@10.0.0.10' \\
  SDN_SSH_OPTS='\-J admin@jump.example' pve\-sdn\-healthcheck
.fi
.RE
.SH CONFIGURATION
All entities auto\-discover; the following are
.B optional
overrides, settable in the environment or in
.IR /etc/pve\-sdn\-healthcheck.conf
(a sourced shell fragment):
.TP
.B SDN_NODES
Space\-separated node host/IPs to iterate (optionally
.IR user @ host ).
.TP
.B SDN_SSH_OPTS
Extra options passed to
.BR ssh (1),
e.g.
.B \-J
for a jump host or
.B \-i
for an identity file.
.TP
.B SDN_VTEPS
Remote VTEP underlay IPs to probe (default: discovered from the EVPN peers).
.TP
.BR SDN_FW_MASTER ", " SDN_FW_BACKUP
Pin the master/backup external BGP peer; a down master is escalated to FAIL,
a down backup to WARN.
.TP
.B SDN_L3VNIS
List of
.IR vxlan_if : vrf : vni
tuples (default: discovered from
.BR "vtysh -c 'show evpn vni'" ).
.TP
.B SDN_MTU_DELTA
Required underlay\-over\-overlay MTU headroom in bytes (default 50; use 70 for
an IPv6 underlay).
.TP
.B SDN_DROP_WINDOW
Seconds used for the live dropped\-packet delta KPI in
.B iface_errors
(default 5; equivalent to
.BR \-\-drop\-window ).
.TP
.B SDN_VRF_PROBES
Optional
.IR vrf : probe_ip
targets enabling a strict data\-plane probe for the L3\-VNI black\-hole check.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
OK \(em all checks passed.
.TP
.B 1
WARN \(em at least one warning, no failures.
.TP
.B 2
CRIT \(em at least one failure.
.TP
.B 3
UNKNOWN \(em usage/dependency error, or a node was unreachable.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
Controller:
.BR bash (1),
.BR ssh (1).
Each node:
.BR vtysh (8)
(FRR),
.BR ip (8),
.BR bridge (8),
.BR sysctl (8).
Optional, used when present:
.BR ethtool (8),
.BR jq (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR pve\-vmnic\-fix (8).
